+++ b/docs/mod-loading/prepared-loading.md
@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+# Experimental prepared resource loading
+
+This branch implements an opt-in native preparation path on the pinned source
+at a7847eae82aaac32175c9a7d199673d5c9323bcd. The user waived the Phase 0
+measurement prerequisite. Existing instrumentation is retained; no game
+performance or rendering acceptance result is implied by that waiver.
+
+## Implemented paths
+
+* Bounded immutable source snapshots, SHA-256 content identity, worker-side
+  lossless decoding for supported WIC layouts, source and decoded cache limits,
+  priorities, cancellation and a reusable worker pool.
+* The real custom-buffer, DDS and WIC loading paths consume prepared memory.
+  Buffers get private mutable copies before legacy resize/override processing.
+* Qualified read-only resources can be prepared on the actual render device
+  during an explicitly declared loading window. GPU identity includes device
+  epoch, source content and effective creation descriptors/options.
+* Production custom shaders use complete six-stage shader/fixed-state bundles;
+  supported full Texture2D SRVs are warmed and reused by exact descriptor and
+  resource identity. Unsupported merge/dynamic state stays on the legacy path.
+* Adapter budget admission, old/new live-object estimates, inactive eviction,
+  active leases, bounded queues and generation fences. Estimates do not prove
+  physical residency or driver memory retirement.
+* Dependency-filtered Windows notifications prepare replacements in the
+  background. Root replacement, overflow and INI changes preserve the explicit
+  legacy reload route. Notifications never activate a replacement or press F10.
+* Detached source identity, bounded lexical IR caching, staged-generation
+  ownership, stale-version rejection and retirement infrastructure.
+
+## Configuration
+
+The default is off. These settings belong in the importer's existing d3dx.ini,
+not in mod files:
+
+    [ModLoading]
+    mode = off
+    cpu_cache_mb = 512
+    gpu_cache_mb = 256
+    max_asset_mb = 64
+    worker_threads = 2
+    max_pending_jobs = 64
+    create_budget_ms = 2
+    upload_budget_mb = 16
+    preparation_loading_window = 0
+    auto_activate = 0
+
+Modes are off, adaptive and prepared_profile. Prepared profile conservatively
+requires every declared resource/shader and an audited command closure to be
+supported, CPU/GPU ready, current and pinned before reporting Ready. Unknown
+operations count as compatibility; a useful prepared hit does not imply that
+the complete profile is ready. Adaptive never reports Ready. CPU cache zero
+disables CPU and dependent GPU preparation; GPU cache zero keeps CPU preparation.
+
+An opt-in background publisher writes bounded scalar diagnostics to
+`.xxmi-preparation/status.json` beside the actual DLL. It includes actual module
+SHA256, PID, timestamp, mode, state and counts. Invalidation tickets prevent old
+readiness updates from replacing newer source/device events. A report can lag
+one writer interval; it is diagnostic and never authorizes activation. Launcher
+reads require authenticated capability metadata, matching DLL hash, fresh data,
+consistent counts and a live reported PID. Status is sampled when settings open
+or Diagnostics is clicked; it is not a continuously refreshed progress display.
+
+GPU creation is admitted only when preparation_loading_window is explicitly
+enabled. Present is not automatically considered a loading screen. Driver calls
+cannot be preempted by the advisory time budget. SINGLETHREADED devices keep
+legacy GPU creation; their CPU cache remains usable.
+
+## Compatibility and remaining work
+
+Unsupported or unproven resource dependencies, mutable outputs, aliases and
+pools retain legacy behavior. Source-only image snapshots may still need decode;
+oversized assets, unknown layouts and device creation failures remain misses.
+Aliased files, reparse points, multiply linked files and unwatchable path forms
+cannot enter readiness; lexical directory watches cannot prove them current.
+Shader creation supports all six stages, but current Windows fixture coverage
+is pixel shader plus an explicit null vertex stage and all four fixed-state
+types. Other nonnull stages require additional qualification.
+
+Current file-change preparation does not publish live resource replacements or
+promote a complete prepared candidate across F10. F10 retains upstream parsing,
+persistence, initialization and reset semantics.
+
+General Phase 5 detached semantic compilation and transactional activation remain
+unfinished. IniHandler still has process-global registries and raw links between
+commands, variables, pools, resources and overrides. Those readers must gain
+generation ownership before live publication is safe. Phase 6 currently checks
+lexical IR equivalence, not full semantic incremental rebuild equivalence.
+CPU and shader caches are bounded in-memory caches. Persistent on-disk derived
+cache reuse is not implemented. Shader compilation remains part of legacy
+configuration parsing; it is not a detached semantic compiler.
+
+Periodic config-closure reconciliation is disabled until an exact closure
+verifier is integrated. Real notifications, overflow recovery and explicit reload
+remain available. Noncooperating multi-file writers do not provide an atomic
+installation boundary.
+
+## Build and verification
+
+Use VS2022 v143 C++ tools and a Windows 10 SDK. Build in an isolated directory
+with all deployment/copy build events disabled. Do not invoke CopyToGames.bat.
+The development launcher repository contains the build script, exact source
+patch and CI workflow. It emits unsigned capability metadata bound to the built
+DLL hash; only the existing authorized package signer can enable the launcher's
+capability gate. No trust override or automatic DLL deployment is added.
+
+Portable tests cover CPU snapshots/cache/scheduling, change reconciliation,
+generation ownership, GPU admission policy and memory PNG parsing. Windows
+fixtures additionally exercise WIC, actual notifications and offscreen WARP
+resources. These are synthetic tests, not actual-game acceptance evidence.
diff --git a/docs/mod-loading/trace-capture.md b/docs/mod-loading/trace-capture.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ddcc553f62db5e4b61c1d79cf5328685eb5426c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/mod-loading/trace-capture.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Phase 0 diagnostic capture
+
+This candidate adds measurement infrastructure only. It does not cache assets,
+change activation or reload semantics, enable a launcher feature, or establish an
+instant-loading result. The baseline source is
+`a7847eae82aaac32175c9a7d199673d5c9323bcd`; retain the candidate patch digest too.
+
+## Capture a short scenario
+
+In the isolated development importer's existing `d3dx.ini`, add these keys to its
+existing `[Logging]` section:
+
+```ini
+mod_load_trace = 1
+mod_load_trace_commands = 0
+```
+
+Start the game, or use its normal F10 reload to arm capture. Perform one short
+scenario. Change `mod_load_trace` to `0`, save, and press F10 again. Disabling an
+active capture queues a dedicated export worker. The worker writes
+`mod-load-trace-<pid>-<tick>.csv` beside the loaded diagnostic DLL. Finish capture
+before exiting the game; process termination does not export the buffer. The
+worker holds a DLL reference until it exits and never joins under the loader
+lock. Configuration changes and worker creation occur during reload, so exclude
+the arm/disarm reloads from steady-state timing comparisons.
+
+The buffer holds 8192 records. There is no continuous background drain. Keep each
+capture short and inspect cumulative `dropped_full` and `dropped_contention` in
+the CSV footer. Loss makes a trace incomplete; it cannot prove zero loading work.
+Counters accumulate over the process lifetime; capture-session IDs distinguish
+enable periods. Command-list recording is off by default because per-draw events
+can fill the buffer within a frame. Enable `mod_load_trace_commands = 1` only for
+short targeted command-list diagnosis. For 100 warm activations, use separate
+short captures as necessary and retain every raw event/sample and loss count.
+
+A failed worker-start/enable request displays a warning. Asynchronous file and
+formatting failures emit debugger diagnostics. If an earlier export is still
+active, allow it to finish and reload again to arm the next capture. File-open
+failure retains queued records; re-enable then disable to retry. A later write
+failure may consume records; preserve partial files and repeat the scenario.
+Persistent consumer-lock contention marks the CSV incomplete and retains the
+records that have not been drained. Output is bounded; it is not a crash recorder.
+
+## What each record means
+
+CSV times are steady-clock CPU nanoseconds, with process-local thread IDs,
+capture-session IDs, start/end frame counters, opaque object addresses, optional
+byte counts, and optional API results. Blank results are unknown, not success.
+Addresses are diagnostic correlation aids only: they can be reused and are not
+asset identities. Frame counters advance after non-test wrapper Present calls;
+multiple swapchains contribute, and no active rendering swapchain has been
+qualified here. Nested durations overlap and must not be summed as independent
+work. No GPU timestamp, residency, frame pacing or driver-preemption claim follows.
+
+Implemented hooks cover resource-section rebuild/discovery, custom buffer
+`ReadFile`, custom shader `D3DCompile`, lazy custom shader/state creation, direct
+custom buffer/texture creation, compatible view creation, configuration reload,
+optional complete command lists, and CPU wall time inside driver Present.
+`file_load_combined` measures DirectXTK texture loading with file reads, decode,
+and device creation combined. Buffer file-open/allocation and texture subphases
+are not isolated. Initial INI parsing before capture is enabled is not captured.
+The reload that disables capture and scopes crossing that transition are omitted.
+
+Other shader-replacement paths, resource copies/pools, context/device lifetimes,
+lock waits, cache coverage, memory budgets and source/dependency identities remain
+unresolved instrumentation work. The API reserves stages for decode, readiness
+wait, activation and externally verified first-correct-frame markers; the current
+integration does not emit these stages. Present or resource creation never
+automatically asserts a correct complete visible mod.
+
+Pair captures with an external frame-time tool and known-correct screenshots or
+video. Preserve the loaded DLL path/hash, compiler/SDK versions, source/patch
+identity, hardware/driver and exact mod/configuration inputs. Follow
+`phase0-baseline-readiness.md` for the blocked Windows/in-game acceptance gate and
+`../../tests/d3d11_fixture/README.md` for the separate synthetic fixture.
