diff --git a/tests/preparation_status/README.md b/tests/preparation_status/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d862662d49e9bfad156264eee9bcd15dbb7c7c8b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/preparation_status/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+Run portable serialization checks with:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/preparation_status/run_tests.py
+```
+
+Windows SDK developer command prompt, from repository root:
+
+```bat
+cl /nologo /std:c++14 /EHsc /W4 /WX /I DirectX11\ModLoading DirectX11\ModLoading\PreparationStatus.cpp DirectX11\ModLoading\SnapshotIO.cpp tests\preparation_status\status_publisher_windows_test.cpp /Fe:status_publisher_windows_test.exe /link ole32.lib windowscodecs.lib propsys.lib
+python tests\preparation_status\run_windows_fixture.py status_publisher_windows_test.exe
+```
+
+The runner owns a temporary output directory until the fixture process exits,
+then validates the bounded JSON, actual executable SHA256, supplied counters,
+explicit Off state, heartbeat age, and absence of leftover temporary files.
+The fixture checks no output before opt-in initialization, Preparing/Ready/Off
+transitions, heartbeat refresh without an update, and invalidation of cached Ready followed
+by a delayed obsolete Ready update with no subsequent authoritative update. It links the publisher
+into its own executable, so module identity/pinning and hashing operate on that
+fixture binary. Eight-second waits and a 35-second child-process timeout bound
+failures. It does not initialize or modify any game directory. Windows execution
+requires CI; portable serialization checks do not qualify Windows file IO.
+
+Production initialization must happen only after explicit feature opt-in and
+outside DllMain. It accepts an address in the publisher's actual module, pins
+that module for process life, and hashes its file once on the background writer
+with SnapshotIO's 64 MiB bound. A heap-owned process service intentionally has
+no shutdown/join path. The worker publishes at approximately 1 Hz through
+status.json.tmp<PID> followed by replacement of status.json. The status object
+contains only Runtime-provided scalar counts/enums and a generic reason; it
+never traverses CustomResource or infers readiness. Update copies at most 256
+reason bytes under a nonblocking try_lock, so a contended update can be dropped;
+Runtime should submit fresh snapshots regularly. Reasons must contain no source
+paths. Serializer escapes controls, bounds reason length, and replaces non-ASCII
+bytes with '?'. Invalid status/digest or file failures yield no fresh status;
+readers must treat absent or stale output as Unknown/offline. IO stalls remain
+on the background thread and never cause an F10/renderer join. Process pinning
+is intentional and must be coordinated with the module initialization contract.
+
+Status publication uses one global ticket counter across F10/runtime rebuilds.
+Runtime must reserve `ReservePreparationStatusTicket()` **before** checking
+source currentness or calculating readiness/counts, then pass that same ticket
+to `UpdatePreparationStatus(status, ticket)`. Source changes and retirement call
+`InvalidatePreparationStatus()`, which atomically raises an invalidation floor
+without acquiring the snapshot mutex. Older updates are rejected, and the
+writer downgrades cached pre-floor non-Off snapshots to Preparing with zero CPU
+and GPU counts even when no subsequent Present/update runs. A later valid
+snapshot can recover with a fresh ticket. The portable pure-fence regression
+holds a simulated snapshot mutex across invalidation and rejects an in-flight
+old Ready ticket after releasing it. Published diagnostics can lag an event by
+one writer interval; they never authorize activation or promise current-frame
+readiness.
